// Pull request author: elhoim
// Change: new rule
// Title: Potential ADCS CA Security Configuration Tampering
// Sigma ID: 35718680-13a9-43ce-96c9-3783edc73103
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: elhoim
// Date: 2026-10-15 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, credential-access, defense-impairment, T1649
// Description: Detects modifications to security-relevant configuration values of an Active Directory
//   Certificate Services (ADCS) Certification Authority on the CA host. Attackers with
//   administrative access to the CA can modify these values to enable
//   "EDITF_ATTRIBUTESUBJECTALTNAME2" via "EditFlags" (ESC6), remove "IF_ENFORCEENCRYPTICERTREQUEST"
//   from "InterfaceFlags" (ESC11) or disable the SID security extension via "DisableExtensionList"
//   (ESC16).
// False positives:
//   - Initial CA installation and configuration
//   - Legitimate CA configuration changes by PKI administrators
// References:
//   - https://www.specterops.io/assets/resources/Certified_Pre-Owned.pdf
//   - https://github.com/ly4k/Certipy/wiki/06-%E2%80%90-Privilege-Escalation
//   - https://blog.compass-security.com/2022/11/relaying-to-ad-certificate-services-over-rpc/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/f669b19474f70bf0caf3142411b7509cf48c96b5/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_adcs_ca_policy_flags_modified.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 1 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\Services\\CertSvc\\Configuration.*$" and (RegistryKey endswith "\\PolicyModules\\CertificateAuthority_MicrosoftDefault.Policy\\DisableExtensionList" or RegistryKey endswith "\\PolicyModules\\CertificateAuthority_MicrosoftDefault.Policy\\EditFlags" or RegistryKey endswith "\\InterfaceFlags")
